course: dictionary
lesson: 12774
title: Editorial: opinion or news?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A newspaper mostly reports the news, which means facts about what has happened. An editorial is different. It is a piece of writing that gives the opinion of the editors, the people in charge of the paper.
explain: «The newspaper's editorial thinks the council should build a new park.» The words thinks and should are clues. The editors are saying what they believe, so this is an opinion, not a fact.
explain: Editorial can also be an adjective, as in «The editorial team met on Monday to choose the stories.» Here it means to do with the people who choose and check what gets published.
fact: An editorial is an article in a newspaper or magazine.
fact: An editorial gives the opinion of the editors, not just the news.
fact: «Editorial» as an adjective means to do with editing, or with the people who choose and check what is published.
fact: News reports give facts. Editorials give views.
fact: An «editorial team» is the group of people who decide what goes into a newspaper or magazine.
exercise: «The editorial said the school day should be shorter.» Is this sentence a fact or an opinion? | A news report | *An opinion | A fact
exercise: Which group is an editorial team? | Shop workers who sell newspapers | *People who choose and check what is published | Readers who write letters | Children who read the paper
exercise: Which piece of writing is an editorial? | A list of the weather for the week | *A piece saying what the editors think about a new bridge | A recipe for cakes | A report of the football score
test: «The editorial team met at nine to decide which stories to print.» What does editorial mean in this sentence? | Something to do with sport | Something to do with cooking | Very old | *To do with editing and choosing what is published
test: «The newspaper's editorial thinks the council should act.» Which word shows that the editorial is giving an opinion? | *thinks | act | Newspaper | council
exam: Which sentence is an editorial rather than a news report? | *«In my opinion, the town needs a new swimming pool, and the council should build one.» | «The council opened a new swimming pool on Monday.» | «Rain is expected across the city tomorrow.» | «The match ended two goals to one.»
